# Git classified the guide PDF as text and warned it would convert its line
# endings on checkout. That commit happened to survive byte-identical, but a
# rebuilt PDF could contain byte sequences that do get mangled, and the file
# would then be silently corrupt for anyone cloning on Windows.
#
# -text disables all end-of-line conversion for these types. Deliberately
# scoped to binaries rather than setting a repo-wide `* text=auto`, which
# would renormalise every existing HTML/CSS/JS file in one noisy commit.

*.pdf   -text
*.png   -text
*.jpg   -text
*.jpeg  -text
*.gif   -text
*.ico   -text
*.webp  -text
*.woff  -text
*.woff2 -text
*.ttf   -text
*.otf   -text
